I think you're reading an awful lot into the tone of the second sentence 
which, I believe, you invented in the first place. It's not in Google's 
archive, anyway. Leave out the word "fucking" and instead of a 
condemnation it's a challenge.

For many people the status quo *is* okay. The fact that the game has not 
been updated in 5 years isn't in itself a problem for them. While there 
are certainly people that *do* feel that 5 years without an update is 
too long, even among that group the subset that want to be programmers 
or designers is a minority so you can expect encouragement from them but 
not (early) help and that encouragement may be expressed as a challenge 
to pick up the gauntlet yourself. And even there, "you" is an 
abstraction that may refer to an unknown or even undefined group rather 
than the specific person to whom it was addressed.

To me, leaving out inferences from the invented tone, those two 
fragments above say:

"I'm not satisfied and I may well branch the project on my own with the 
help of a few like-minded people."

and 

"If you're not satisfied, why don't you gather a few like-minded people 
and branch the project on your own?"

